e_%28104015%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Nordnes Park","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.39758,"lo":5.30782,"d":508,"ds":"The Nordnes Park (Norwegian: Nordnesparken) is a public park in Bergen Municipality in Vestland county, Norway. The park is located near the centre of the city of Bergen on the northwestern end of the Nordnes peninsula. It was established in 1888-1898 after an initiative from Edvard G. Johannessen in Det nyttige Selskab.","wpu":"Nordnes Park","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Nordnes%2C_Bergen%2C_Hodaland%2C_Norway_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Nordnes%2C_Bergen%2C_Hodaland%2C_Norway_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Komediehuset på Engen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.3918,"lo":5.3177,"d":579,"ds":"Komediehuset på Engen ('Meadow Comedy House') was a historic theatre in Bergen in Norway, active between 1800 and 1909. It was the likely first theatre building in Norway.","wpu":"Komediehuset på Engen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Komediehuset_p%C3%A5_Engen_%E2%80%93_Bergen_The_old_theatre.jpg/960px-Komediehuset_p%C3%A5_Engen_%E2%80%93_Bergen_The_old_theatre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"The Blue Stone","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.391882,"lo":5.322893,"d":654,"ds":"The Blue Stone (Norwegian: Den blå stein) is a monument in the city of Bergen, Norway. The stone is nine meters (30 feet) long, and made of Brazilian sodalite. It is resting on a stone block, which gives it a characteristic inclination towards the northeast.","wpu":"The Blue Stone","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Kong_Olav_Vs_plass_4%2C_Bergen%2C_2019_%2801%29.jpg/960px-Kong_Olav_Vs_plass_4%2C_Bergen%2C_2019_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bergen Aquarium","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.3997,"lo":5.3038,"d":784,"ds":"Bergen Aquarium (Norwegian: 'Akvariet i Bergen') is a public aquarium in Bergen, Norway. It is situated on the Nordnes peninsula and is one of Bergen's tourist attractions.","wpu":"Bergen Aquarium","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Entrance_Akvariet_i_Bergen_%282022%29.jpg/960px-Entrance_Akvariet_i_Bergen_%282022%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Permanenten","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.390627,"lo":5.324147,"d":810,"ds":"Permanenten (Norwegian: Permanenten Vestlandske kunstindustrimuseum), formerly the West Norway Museum of Decorative Art, also referred to as KODE 1, is a museum in Bergen, Norway. The museum is part of the KODE Art Museums and Composer Homes and was originally established in 1887 at the initiative of Johan Bøgh.","wpu":"Permanenten","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/KODE_1%2C_Bergen%2C_2019_%2801%29.jpg/960px-KODE_1%2C_Bergen%2C_2019_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bergen Cathedral","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.393875,"lo":5.33085,"d":836,"ds":"Bergen Cathedral (Norwegian: Bergen domkirke) is a cathedral in the city of Bergen in Vestland county, Norway. It is the episcopal seat of the Church of Norway's Diocese of Bjørgvin as well as the seat of the \"Bergen domkirke\" parish and the seat of the Bergen domprosti (arch-deanery). It is part of the Church of Norway.","wpu":"Bergen Cathedral","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/11/Bergen_domkirken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"St John's Church, Bergen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.388527,"lo":5.319344,"d":950,"ds":"St. John's Church (Norwegian: Johanneskirken) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Bergen Municipality in Vestland county, Norway. It is located in the Sydnes area of the city of Bergen.","wpu":"St John's Church, Bergen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Johanneskirken%2C_Bergen%2C_Noruega%2C_2019-09-08%2C_DD_71.jpg/960px-Johanneskirken%2C_Bergen%2C_Noruega%2C_2019-09-08%2C_DD_71.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bergen Kunsthall","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.3897,"lo":5.3265,"d":965,"ds":"Bergen Kunsthall is a contemporary art centre in Bergen, Norway, that organises and hosts exhibitions and events by both Norwegian and international artists. Since 1953, Bergen Kunsthall has curated and produced the annual Festspillutstillingen, which is now regarded as one of Norway’s most prestigious solo exhibitions. Their 2017 exhibition \"BRIDGIT\" by Charlotte Prodger won the Turner Prize in 2018.","wpu":"Bergen Kunsthall","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Bergen_kunsthall.jpg/960px-Bergen_kunsthall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sandvik Church","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.405388,"lo":5.325485,"d":1042,"ds":"Sandvik Church (Norwegian: Sandvikskirken) is a parish church of the Church of Norway in Bergen Municipality in Vestland county, Norway. It is located in the Sandviken neighborhood in the city of Bergen. It is the church for the Sandviken parish, which is part of the Bergen domprosti (arch-deanery) in the Diocese of Bjørgvin.","wpu":"Sandvik Church","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Sandvikskirken_Bergen_2009_1.JPG/960px-Sandvikskirken_Bergen_2009_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Grieg Hall","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":60.388858,"lo":5.328214,"d":1095,"ds":"Grieg Hall (Norwegian: Grieghallen) is a 1,500-seat concert hall located on Edvard Griegs plass (square) in Bergen, Norway. Grieghallen was named in honor of Bergen-born composer Edvard Grieg, who served as music director of the Bergen Philharmonic Orchestra from 1880 until 1882. It serves as the home of the Bergen Philharmonic Orchestra.","wpu":"Grieg Hall","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Grieghallen%2C_Bergen%2C_Noruega%2C_2019-09-08%2C_DD_65.jpg/960px-Grieghallen%2C_Bergen%2C_Noruega%2C_2019-09-08%2C_DD_65.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Bergen (Norwegian pronunciation: [ˈbæ̀rɡən] , locally [ˈbæ̂ʁgæn]) is a city and municipality in the Vestland county on the west coast of Norway. Bergen is the second-largest city in Norway after the capital, Oslo. At the beginning of 2026, the population was 294,860, according to Statistics Norway.","wpu":"Bergen","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Bergen_panorama_at_night_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg/960px-Bergen_panorama_at_night_-_panoramio_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}